From 8fee242ca0e5cb30f5a1c52fc75b8a07a84e0067 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:59:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Transport: Back a TCP connect up after 250ms, as browsers do

A connect whose SYN was lost waited for the kernel to send it again after
1s. DialSystem now starts one backup connect beside a TCP connect that
has not answered after 250ms, as Chrome's and Firefox's connection pools
do, and uses the first connection made; the other attempt is cancelled
and a connection it makes anyway is closed. A refused connect is an
answer and starts no backup. Only the connect is backed up: a TLS or
REALITY handshake on top of it still has its one connection, so a
handshake that hangs sends no second ClientHello.

On a stand that drops the first 200ms of SYNs to the target, a connect
through freedom took 1.007s and now 0.252s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
